## 7) Boot Sequence

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant B as Bootstrap (host)
    participant M as main.ts (Node.js)
    participant K as Kernel.ts (Dinawari)
    participant F as BKFS (SQLite)
    participant I as /bin/init.ts (PID 1)
    participant S as /bin/tsh.ts (shell)
    participant W as Asteracea (WM)

    Note over B: bootstrap.sh / .bat
    B->>M: node src/main.ts
    M->>K: new Kernel() + kernel.boot()

    activate K
    K->>F: mount / (BKFS)
    K->>K: process /etc/fstab.json<br/>(mount /tmp ramfs, /mnt/host ...)
    K->>K: init TTYs + register devices
    K->>K: serial auto-detect + HAL drivers<br/>+ pre-compile framework libs
    K->>K: ensure default auth & groups
    K-->>M: boot complete
    deactivate K

    M->>K: kernel.runInit()
    K->>I: spawn process (PID 1)

    activate I
    I->>I: run /etc/rc.local (start daemons)
    alt GUI login
        I->>W: launch asteracea (WM) → desktop
        activate W
        Note over W: Taskbar, launcher, pinned apps
        deactivate W
    else TTY login
        I->>S: login → /bin/tsh.ts (shell)
        activate S
        Note over S: User session active
        deactivate S
    end
    deactivate I
```

## 8) Alur Syscall & IPC

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    APP["App (Worker Thread)"]
    UL["UserLib (libc-like)"]
    IPC["IPC postMessage / SEND_MSG"]
    SC["Syscall Dispatcher (main thread)"]
    K["Kernel services"]
    GR["GUIRegistry"]
    DOME["DOME (display server)"]
    BK["BKFS / Devices / Scheduler"]

    APP -->|syscall call| UL
    APP <-->|worker IPC| IPC
    UL -->|dispatch SyscallCode| SC
    SC -->|route| BK
    SC -->|GUI_REQ| GR
    BK -->|return| SC
    GR --> DOME
    SC -->|response postMessage| UL
    UL --> APP
```
